course: dictionary
lesson: 2258
title: Crazes and fads
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A craze is something that suddenly becomes very popular for a short time, then fades away. The context gives you clues. In «Jack spends his whole £10 on the fidget toy everyone has, and two days later nobody cares about fidget toys any more», the words "everyone has" show it is popular, and "nobody cares" two days later shows it does not last.
explain: Now read «Toad has a new craze, and for days he'll be useless.» Toad is so keen on his new interest that nothing else matters for days. Swap in the meaning: "Toad has a new fad, and for days he'll be useless" still makes sense, so craze fits here.
explain: Look for the phrases that often go with it: «the latest craze», «a craze for», and «craze took off». If you see «crazed» instead, it is a different use. «The crowd was crazed with fear» means wild and out of control with fear.
fact: A craze is something that suddenly becomes very popular for a short time, like a toy, game or dance.
fact: «The latest craze» means the newest thing that everyone wants.
fact: Crazes spread quickly, such as «short viral dances» that travel fast online.
fact: Craze can also be a rare verb meaning to make someone wild or mad, usually seen as «crazed».
fact: When glaze on pottery or glass crazes, it gets a pattern of tiny cracks.
exercise: Toad's sailing, punting and house-boating each lasted only a short time. What is each one for Toad? | *A craze | A lazy nap | A long journey | A cracked pot
exercise: «Craze took off» in the playground means the fad did what? | *Spread fast and became popular | Went quiet at once | Cracked into tiny pieces | Stopped for ever
exercise: «The crowd was crazed with fear.» What does crazed suggest? | Full of cheerful songs | Tidy and clean | Calm and sleepy | *Wild and out of control with fear
test: In «Toad has a new craze», which word tells you the craze has only just started? | Days | *New | Toad | Craze
test: A pot whose glaze crazes gets what? | A heavy weight | A bright glow | *Tiny cracks | Shiny colours
exam: Which word best names something everyone wants for a short time, then quickly forgets? | Habit | Anthem | Tradition | *Craze
